

Some notes about GNU Radio


1- On the right side, we can see that we have many block
like audio, filters,...
    - these are the top level block
    - each block is organised also into nested blocks

- When we open GNU radio, we have directly 2 blocks inserted for us:
1 The 'Options block'
  - we double click on it and select QT for the interface
  - this is important because when we select the block on the right side, it will also give us the choice which type of GUI we want

2- The 'variable block' select the sample rate for us
    - if we grab some block for example, like 'Signal Source', and double click, we can see that the sample rate in signal source matche the sample rate in variable block
    - and every other block will have the same sampling rate as in the 'variable block'
  